    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1249">

                <pb facs="1291" n="1279" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg1279"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">767.68119/11–1645: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-11-16T19:00:00+00:00">November 16,
                            1945—7 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 16—6 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>12034. Deptel 9545, October 30.<anchor n="97" xml:id="d1249-f1"/> Regarding
                    Straits question Foreign Office official told us today that the Turks had asked
                    the British <pb facs="1292" n="1280" xml:id="pg1280"/> for their comments on US
                    note of November 2 to the Turkish Govt. Reply has been drafted (but not yet
                    finally approved in Foreign Office) stating that British would of course be glad
                    to attend a conference for the revision of Montreux Convention and that the
                    British prefer to withhold their comments on US note until conference; official
                    remarked the points in American note seemed satisfactory.</p>
                <p>Sent Dept as 12034; repeated Ankara 125 and Moscow 390.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1249-f1" n="97" xml:id="d1249-f1-content">
                <p>Same as telegram 1049 to Ankara, <ref target="#pg1265">p. 1265</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
